      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(memory-host-sdk): prevent mid-transcript [cron:] from wiping archive content",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nMid-transcript user messages starting with `[cron:...]` (e.g. asking about a failed cron job) triggered the cron classifier and wiped the entire archive content. Real cron prompts are always the first message; user-typed `[cron:]` appears later and must not wipe.\n\nCloses #98241\n\n## Root Cause / Fix\n\n`buildSessionEntry` in the memory host SDK checked `isGeneratedCronPromptMessage` on EVERY user message. Any message matching `[cron:*]` reset the collector, discarding all previously collected content.\n\nFix: gate the cron classifier on `collected.length === 0` so only the first message triggers cron classification.\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Real `buildSessionEntry` proof — mid-transcript [cron:] content survives\n\n```\npnpm test packages/memory-host-sdk/src/host/session-files.test.ts\n  buildSessionEntry\n    ✓ preserves prior content when [cron:] appears mid-transcript (regression for #98241)\n      → Content from before [cron:] survives (\"Acme\", \"budget is 5000\")\n  Tests  38 passed (38)\n```\n\n## Change Type\n- [x] Bug fix\n## Scope\n- [x] memory-host-sdk\n## Security Impact\n- New permissions? No · Secrets changed? No · New network calls? No",
        "branch": "fix/98241-cron-prefix-archive-wipe",
